/**
 * \namespace graphics
 * \brief Root namespace for the graphics engine.
 *
 * Contains all engine subsystems, including:
 * - graphics::core (diagnostics, logging, error handling)
 * - graphics::platform (platform abstraction and backend selection)
 *
 * This namespace itself does not contain code directly; it serves as the
 * top-level grouping for all engine modules.
 */
namespace graphics;

/**
 * \namespace graphics::core
 * \brief Core diagnostics, logging, and error-handling subsystem.
 *
 * The graphics::core namespace provides the foundational error-reporting
 * and diagnostic facilities used throughout the engine. This includes
 * diagnostic message representation, subsystem categorization, log levels,
 * logging interfaces, and lightweight error/expected-value utilities.
 *
 * # Responsibilities
 *
 * ## Diagnostics
 * - Diagnostic message structure (Diagnostic)
 * - Source-location-aware error reporting
 * - Diagnostic categories (DiagnosticCategory)
 * - Severity levels (LogLevel)
 *
 * These components provide a unified mechanism for describing and reporting
 * errors, warnings, and informational messages across all engine subsystems.
 *
 * ## Logging
 * - Logging interface and helpers (logging.hpp)
 * - Integration with diagnostic messages
 *
 * Logging is built on top of the diagnostic system and provides a consistent
 * way to emit structured messages during engine execution.
 *
 * ## Error and Status Handling
 * - Status codes (status.hpp)
 * - Expected-value type (expected.hpp)
 *
 * These utilities support expressive and lightweight error propagation
 * without relying on exceptions, enabling predictable control flow and
 * efficient error handling.
 *
 * # Notes
 * - All engine subsystems should use these facilities for reporting errors
 *   and diagnostics.
 * - Higher-level modules (rendering, math, platform) depend on this layer.
 * - This namespace forms the foundation of the engine's reliability model.
 *
 * \see graphics
 */
 namespace graphics::core{}

/**
 * \namespace graphics::platform
 * \brief Platform abstraction layer of the graphics engine.
 *
 * The graphics::platform namespace defines the interfaces and backend
 * selection mechanisms used to interact with the underlying operating
 * system and windowing environment. This layer isolates platform-specific
 * behavior behind a clean, engine-facing API.
 *
 * # Responsibilities
 *
 * ## Platform Interface
 * - i_platform — abstract interface representing the platform backend
 *
 * The platform interface defines the minimal set of operations required by
 * the engine, such as initialization, shutdown, window creation, and event
 * polling. All platform backends must implement this interface.
 *
 * ## Backend Selection
 * - backend.hpp — backend enumeration and selection helpers
 *
 * This component provides the mechanism for choosing which platform
 * implementation to use (e.g., GLFW, Win32, SDL). It allows the engine to
 * remain backend-agnostic while supporting multiple windowing systems.
 *
 * # Design Goals
 * - Provide a stable, minimal API for platform interaction
 * - Allow multiple backend implementations without changing engine code
 * - Keep platform-specific details isolated from higher-level systems
 *
 * # Notes
 * - All platform backends must implement i_platform.
 * - Backend selection is performed through the facilities in backend.hpp.
 * - Higher-level systems (rendering, diagnostics, input) depend on this
 *   namespace for window creation and event dispatch.
 *
 * \see graphics
 * \see graphics::core
 */
 namespace graphics::platform;
